    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d65">

                <pb facs="0073" n="61" xml:id="pg61"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">033.1110 Wallace, Henry A./110: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Scotten</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1943-03-18"
                            >March 18, 1943</date>.<lb/>[Received March 18—2:03 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>240. For Coordinator for Jamieson from Gaudet.<anchor n="13" xml:id="d65-f1"/>
                    One greatest receptions ever arranged for visiting dignitary now completed for
                    Wallace who arriving plane 11:00 this morning. Cooperating with Government’s
                    declaration national holiday all merchants closing stores his honor, all schools
                    closed and thousands young school children will line streets welcome Wallace.
                    Papers increased sizes order carry full page ads, editorials, front page news
                    stories on Wallace’s visit. Taking on carnival spirits, city bedecked with
                    canopy American, Costa Rican flags. [Gaudet.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Scotten</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d65-f1" n="13" xml:id="d65-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram was a message from one official to another of the office of the
                    Coordinator of Inter-American Affairs.</p>
            </note>
